        ("Your head", [
            "To make your head, Some Wins takes a few photos with the front camera, or uses one photo you choose from your library. Apple's tools, on your device, find your face and the points of it (eyes, brows, mouth and jaw) to cut it out and choose the frames it keeps. Choosing a photo for your head does not give Some Wins your library: iOS hands over only the one you pick. It keeps those small cut-out pictures and, with each, where the eyes sit, their outline and their colour, so your head can blink. It never keeps video, never makes or keeps a faceprint or anything that could recognise you, and does not keep the other points it found. Some Wins cannot see any of it. Your head is your picture in Some Wins: it appears in Profile, on your Wins tab and your map, and in your crews, and it is offered as a sticker on your photos. Delete This Head takes it out of use. It stays on this device with your last three heads, and is never sent, until you choose Delete for Good on it in Profile or reset all data.",
